==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|is|non|hverr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hweraz}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|is|/xʷɛːr/}}
* {{IPA|is|/kʰvɛːr/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ɛːr|s=1}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|hvers|hverir|pl2=hverar}}

# a [[hot spring]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s2|hv|e|r|}}
Previously also declined according to the first declension, with plural ''hverar'':
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|hv|e|r}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|hot spring}} {{l|is|laug}}, {{l|is|heit laug}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|goshver}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|is|lind}}
* {{l|is|heitur pottur}}
* {{l|is|pottur}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|is|non|hverr}} (from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwarjaz}}) and {{m|non|*hver}} (from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwaz}}), which were conflated in (late) Old Norse. Most of the inflected forms of *''hwaz'' have since become obsolete, and what remains in form is essentially the descendant of *''hwarjaz'', but with an extra form for the neuter nominative and accusative singular: ''hvað'' from Old Norse {{m|non|hvat}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|is|hvur}}, {{l|is|hvör}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|is|/kʰvɛːr/|/kʰvʏːr/|/xʷɛːr/|/kʰvœːr/}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|hver|neuter|hvert|or|hvað}}

# {{lb|is|interrogative}} [[who]], [[what]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Hver''' er ég?|'''Who''' am I?}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Hver''' [[stela|stal]] [[kaka#Icelandic|kökunni]] úr krúsinni í gær?|'''Who''' stole the cookie from the jar last night?}}
# {{lb|is|interrogative}} [[which]] (referring to one or several of more than two things or persons; may be qualified by a noun phrase in genitive or a noun phrase with the preposition {{m|is|af||of}})
#: {{ux|is|'''Hver''' þeirra [[finnast|finnst]] þér bestur, hvíti, græni eða appelsínuguli [[bíll]]inn?|'''Which''' of these do you like best, the white, the green{{,}} or the orange car?}}
# {{lb|is|interrogative|neuter singular}} [[what]], which part (referring to part of a mass or group of things or people considered collectively; may be qualified by a noun phrase with the preposition {{m|is|af||of}})
#: {{ux|is|Við verðum að [[ákveða]] '''hvað''' af landinu við viljum [[vernda]] fyrir [[snjóflóð]].|We have to decide '''which part''' of the land we want to protect from avalanches.}}
# {{lb|is|relative}} [[whichever]] (of more than two things or persons; followed by a relative clause; may be qualified by a noun phrase in genitive or a noun phrase with the preposition {{m|is|af||of}})
#: {{ux|is|'''Hver''' sem ég [[tala]]ði við í dag var í góðu [[skap]]i.|'''Whoever''' I talked to today was in a good mood.}}
# {{lb|is|relative|neuter singular}} [[whatever]] (followed by a relative clause; may be qualified by a noun phrase with the preposition {{m|is|af||of}})
#: {{ux|is|'''Hvað''' sem ég [[reyna|reyndi]], það [[takast|tókst]] ekki.|'''Whatever''' I tried, it didn't work.}}
# {{lb|is|relative|chiefly|archaic}} [[who]], [[which]], [[that]] (used in the forming of relative clauses)
# {{lb|is|indefinite}} [[each]], [[every]]
#: {{ux|is|Besta [[w:rúgbrauð|rúgbrauðið]] kemur frá [[w:Hveragerði|Hveragerði]]. Það [[vita|veit]] '''hver''' íslendingur.|The best ‘rye bread’ is from Hveragerði. '''Every''' Icelander knows that.}}
#* ''Article 1'', [[Universal Declaration of Human Rights]] ([http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=ice Icelandic], [http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=eng English])
#*: {{quote|is|'''Hver''' maður er borinn frjáls og jafn öðrum að virðingu og réttindum. Menn eru gæddir vitsmunum og samvizku, og ber þeim að breyta bróðurlega hverjum við annan.|'''All''' human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights. They are endowed with reason and conscience and should act towards one another in a spirit of brotherhood.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The neuter form ''hvað'' is used with senses 1, 3{{,}} and 5, ''hvert'' with the others. Compare also {{l|is|hvor|hvor, hvort|which (of two)}}.

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-pron-hver}}

